{"kind":"assert","text":"J5's source is at its gate, at the merge of main 8851f19d. The wake is `dap issue wait`, over the room's existing head stream, with no hosted MCP. The local witness passed on wrangler dev. No deployed run has happened.\n\nOne clause needs your ruling. An absent person returning on another device: only the Page redeems a device-key link, and that key stays in the browser, where apps/views cannot use it. `dap join` does not accept the link. So a person cannot put a second device's key under the CLI or the views by real commands. The native test and the witness compose invite-key and enrol for that step.\n\nRecommendation: file a separate request for `dap join` to accept a device-key link. invitations.ts holds retained originals and sealed code, so it deserves its own review, and J5 lands without it. The deployed witness then runs the second device on the Page, or waits for that request. Say which, and whether J5's deployed run waits for it.\n\nTwo more for your information: review marks stay on one device, so a new device lists every scope again and the card says so. I recommend leaving that until someone asks. And J5 needs a room created with --cohort commons, with the Brief issue definition active and issue.approve and issue.decide on the roles, for its deployed run.","body":{"request":"067ae4f843a0e3ca9fcd6364041800e724be3c5d"}}